        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">The UGC market is shifting. Several trends are reshaping which niches will be most valuable in the next 12&ndash;18 months.</p>

        <ul class="pl-5 mb-4 space-y-2 text-ink-2">
          <li><strong>AI tool UGC is exploding.</strong> Every AI startup needs UGC content to stand out. The volume of AI products launching is unprecedented, and most lack in-house creative teams. Creators who can demo AI tools naturally are in extreme demand.</li>
          <li><strong>B2B UGC is going mainstream.</strong> Enterprise software, professional services, and B2B platforms are adopting UGC-style ads. This was a tiny niche 18 months ago. It&rsquo;s now a significant and growing opportunity with premium rates.</li>
          <li><strong>Sustainability reporting is creating content demand.</strong> New EU and US sustainability reporting requirements mean brands need authentic sustainability content at scale. This isn&rsquo;t just marketing &mdash; it&rsquo;s compliance-driven demand.</li>
          <li><strong>Health and wellness content is fragmenting.</strong> The broad &ldquo;health&rdquo; niche is splitting into sub-niches: mental health apps, sleep tech, gut health, longevity supplements. Sub-niche specialists are emerging and commanding premium rates.</li>
          <li><strong>Creator-brand retainers are replacing one-off deals.</strong> Across all niches, brands are moving toward monthly retainer agreements with fewer, more trusted creators instead of one-off projects with many creators. This benefits niche specialists who build deep brand relationships.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

